<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dido</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elissa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dido, also called Elissa, was the legendary queen from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> who is said to have founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. According to tradition, she fled her brother Pygmalion and established the city on the North African coast. Her story became the foundation legend of Carthage and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, and was later retold in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeneid">Aeneid</a>.</p></div>
